@startuml DB-DeveloperWorkflow
' ============================================================
' Diagram: Developer Database Change Workflow
' Purpose: Shows the full developer inner loop: making schema
'          changes, testing locally, committing version.json,
'          and handing off to BuildMaster for CI ingestion.
' Author:  Generated for Sprint-0007
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #888888

title "Developer Database Change Workflow\n(Schema edit → Local test → Commit → BuildMaster CI ingestion)"

|Developer Workstation|
start

:Open sprint worktree\nin VS Code;
note right
  Branch: <sprint-number>-Sprint-NNNN-work-items
  Repo:   ATAP.Utilities-wt-NNN-Sprint-NNNN-work-items
end note

:Edit Database/Flyway/SQL/\nV00.01.NNNNNN__*.sql\n(new versioned migration);
note right
  Follows naming convention:
  V<Major>.<Minor>.<NNNNNN>__<Description>.sql
  Major.Minor match version.json
end note

if (Schema change?) then (yes)
  :Edit V*.sql DDL\n(ALTER TABLE / CREATE TABLE /\nADD CONSTRAINT, etc.);
else (data / seed change)
  :Edit Data/*.csv\nor adjust R__*.sql\n(repeatable migration);
endif

:Edit db/<App>/releases/<ver>.yml\n(per-release change-unit manifest:\n- dbChangeUnit name\n- flywayTargetVersion\n- list of migration files + checksums);

|Developer Workstation|
:Run Rebuild-All.ps1\n(targets: Experimental + Development DBs);
note right
  Script calls:
  1. Invoke-DatabaseProvisioning (dbatools drop/create)
  2. Invoke-Flyway.ps1 (flyway migrate)
  3. Runs V*.sql, R*.sql, *.csv seed loading
end note

if (Flyway migrate succeeds?) then (yes)
  :Run local Pester tests\n(DbManifestSchema.Tests.ps1);
  note right
    Tests validate:
    - Table schemas match expected definitions
    - Seed data row counts
    - Constraint names
    - Migration checksum integrity
  end note
  if (Pester tests pass?) then (yes)
    :Optionally run ad-hoc queries\nin Database/Queries/ to validate data;
  else (fail)
    :Fix failing test or schema\n→ loop back;
    :Edit V*.sql / R*.sql / *.csv;
    stop
  endif
else (fail)
  :Read Flyway error output;
  :Fix migration script;
  stop
endif

|Developer Workstation|
:Commit changes to sprint branch\n(all modified Database/** files);
note right
  Committed files may include:
  - Database/Flyway/SQL/V*.sql
  - Database/Flyway/Data/*.csv
  - Database/Flyway/SQL/R*.sql
  - db/<App>/releases/<ver>.yml
  - Do NOT commit version.json yet
    (NBGV derives version from commit height)
end note

:Verify local build one more time:\nNew-DatabaseChangePackage -Tier Experimental;
note right
  Packs ATAPUtilities.Database.nupkg
  with NBGV-derived pre-release version.
  Verifies all files included correctly.
end note

if (Package builds cleanly?) then (yes)
  ' Trigger CI
  :git push to sprint branch origin;
  note right
    GitHub webhook fires →
    BuildMaster "DB: Experimental" stage triggered.
    Developer does not need to do anything else.
  end note
else (no)
  :Fix packaging issue;
  stop
endif

|BuildMaster (CI)|
:Receive Git webhook\n(DB/** path filter matches);

:Stage: Experimental\n1. Resolve feed name\n2. New-DatabaseChangePackage (pack)\n3. Push to nuget-experimental;

:Invoke-Flyway.ps1\n→ Experimental SQL Server DB;

if (Flyway + smoke tests pass?) then (yes)
  :Promote to Development stage\n(Move-ProGetPackage → nuget-development);
  :Invoke-Flyway.ps1\n→ Development SQL Server DB;
  if (Full Pester suite passes?) then (yes)
    :Queue Integration stage;
    note right
      Integration + QA + Production
      follow the promotion pipeline
      (see DB-PromotionPipeline-BuildMaster-ProGet).
    end note
  else (fail)
    :Notify developer:\nCI failure in Development stage;
    |Developer Workstation|
    :Investigate CI failure\n(check BM build log);
    stop
  endif
else (fail)
  :Notify developer:\nCI failure in Experimental stage;
  |Developer Workstation|
  :Fix migration and push again;
  stop
endif

|Developer Workstation|
:Monitor BuildMaster progress\n(Experimental → Development → Integration);

:All stages green?;
note right
  Developer's sprint task is complete
  when Integration stage passes.
  QA and Production gates are
  separate human-approval steps.
end note

stop

@enduml
